1367-<section class="ltx_section" id="S6">
1368-<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">
1369-<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Constructing extremal maxout polytopes</h2>
1370-<div class="ltx_para" id="S6.p1">
1371-<p class="ltx_p">In Section <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S3" title="3 Boxtopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we found that boxtopes with extremal f-vector are neighborly cubical polytopes.
1372-This section goes beyond boxtopes.
1373-We discuss methods for constructing maxout polytopes of type <math alttext="(d,n,m)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p1.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> with the maximum possible number of vertices.
1374-Our results are for zonoboxtopes, which is the case <math alttext="m=1" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p1.m2" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
1375:This is generalized to any <math alttext="m" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p1.m3" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> in Conjecture <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Conjecture 6.6. â€£ 6 Constructing extremal maxout polytopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>.</p>
1376-</div>
1377-<div class="ltx_para" id="S6.p2">
1378-<p class="ltx_p">Recall that a <math alttext="(d,n)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n)</annotation></semantics></math>-zonoboxtope <math alttext="Q" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m2" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a maxout polytope of type <math alttext="(d,n,1)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m3" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can write</p>
1379-<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table" id="S6.E24">
1380-<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1381-<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1382-<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math alttext="Q\,\,=\,\,\operatorname{conv}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}I_{i}\,\,\cup\,\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}I_{i}\right)\,\,\subset\,\,\mathbb{R}^{d}," class="ltx_Math" display="block" id="S6.E24.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>â¡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">âˆ‘</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">â€‹</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.385em">âˆª</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">âˆ‘</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">â€‹</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">âŠ‚</mo><msup><mi>â„</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\,\,=\,\,\operatorname{conv}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}I_{i}\,\,\cup\,\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}I_{i}\right)\,\,\subset\,\,\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
