ai/maxout\paper\agy_note_review.log:24:2. **[Minor] Computational Engine Detail:** In Section 2.4, you mention "exact kernel computations in the quotient ring" and verification "modulo the Grassmann-PlÃ¼cker ideal." A mathematically curious reader might appreciate a half-sentence or a parenthetical specifying the computational algebraic method used for this ideal membership test (e.g., standard GrÃ¶bner bases over $\mathbb{Q}$) since it is the engine of the 57,637 non-trivial certificates. 
ai/maxout\paper\agy_note_review.log:8:The narrative is a perfectly faithful distillation of the underlying proof chain. It accurately covers the chamber model, the enumeration of the 33,140 valid patterns, the reduction to a single orbit of 384 chirotopes, the critical $D_5$ symmetry reduction to four split representatives (specifically emphasizing the non-equivalence of the two 2-subset orbits), the cell-wide polynomial Gordan certificates modulo the Grassmann-PlÃ¼cker ideal, and the parity/perturbation endgame.
