1387:<p class="ltx_p">where <math alttext="I_{i}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m4" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>âŠ‚</mo><msup><mi>â„</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a line segment, and <math alttext="a_{i},b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m5" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>âˆˆ</mo><msub><mi>â„</mi><mrow><mi></mi><mo>â‰¥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math alttext="i\in[n]" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p2.m6" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>âˆˆ</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>.
1388:Note that (<a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S6.E24" title="In 6 Constructing extremal maxout polytopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) generalizes (<a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S2.E5" title="In 2 From Networks to Polytopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
1389:</div>
1390:<div class="ltx_para" id="S6.p3">
1391:<p class="ltx_p">We now give a tight upper bound on the number of edges of a zonoboxtope for <math alttext="d=2" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p3.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1392:</div>
1393:<div class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem" id="S6.Thmtheorem1">
1394:<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem">
1395:<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span>
1396:</h6>
1397:<div class="ltx_para" id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1">
1398:<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The number of edges (equivalently, vertices) of a <math alttext="(2,n)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,n)</annotation></semantics></math>-zonoboxtope is at most <math alttext="\,2n+4\lfloor n/2\rfloor" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>â€‰2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">â€‹</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">â€‹</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">âŒŠ</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">âŒ‹</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,2n+4\lfloor n/2\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.
1399:This upper bound is tight for all <math alttext="n\geq 2" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>â‰¥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
1400:</div>
1401:</div>
1402:<div class="ltx_para" id="S6.p4">
1403:<p class="ltx_p">Lemma <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 6.2. â€£ 6 Constructing extremal maxout polytopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> gives an alternative characterization of <math alttext="Q" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p4.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.
1404:It is instrumental in the proof of Theorem <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21286v1#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. â€£ 6 Constructing extremal maxout polytopes â€£ Maxout Polytopes"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> and in generating examples of zonoboxtopes with maximal f-vector for <math alttext="d\geq 2" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.p4.m2" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>â‰¥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1405:</div>
1406:<div class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma" id="S6.Thmtheorem2">
