1411:<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math alttext="Q" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math alttext="(d,n)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n)</annotation></semantics></math>-zonoboxtope. There exist <math alttext="a_{1}^{\prime},b_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{n}^{\prime},b_{n}^{\prime},\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" class="ltx_math_unparsed" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>â€²</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>â€²</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">â€¦</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>â€²</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>â€²</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">âˆˆ</mo><msub><mi>â„</mi><mrow><mi></mi><mo>â‰¥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{\prime},b_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{n}^{\prime},b_{n}^{\prime},\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and pairwise non-parallel line segments <math alttext="I_{1},\ldots,I_{n}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">â€¦</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1},\ldots,I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>â„</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that
